  "body": "Following up https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/8653 per @emilio's and @tabatkins's suggestion, I'm asking for the [8.1.3.4 Enabling and disabling scripting](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#enabling-and-disabling-scripting) paragraph to take in account CSP `script-src none`, e.g. by adding the the following text to the last bullet point under _\"Scripting is enabled for an [environment settings object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#environment-settings-object) settings when all of the following conditions are true:\"_ (before the full stop):\r\n\r\n> [...] and settings's [global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-settings-object-global)'s [CSP list](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#global-object-csp-list) does not include any policy whose [directive set](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#policy-directive-set) [contains](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain) a [directive](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#directives) whose name is \"[script-src](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#sandbox)\" and whose value is \"none\"\r\n",
